<main class="page" role="main">
  <h1>Tiro Finance Sync — Privacy</h1>
  <p class="caption">privacy notice for a personal, non-commercial banking sync</p>

  <p>
    Tiro Finance Sync is a personal tool built and operated by Davide Pucci
    to synchronize his own bank accounts into his own budgeting software.
    it is not offered to anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>what is collected</h2>
  <p>
    through the Enable Banking API, with explicit consent renewed via the
    bank's own login, the tool reads: account identifiers, balances and
    transaction history. access is strictly read-only — it cannot move money,
    open products or change anything at the bank.
  </p>

  <h2>where it goes</h2>
  <p>
    data is stored on a private server operated by Davide Pucci
    (finance.davidepucci.it) and used solely to categorize spending and
    produce personal finance reports. it is never sold, shared with
    advertisers or disclosed to third parties, except Enable Banking as the
    technical API intermediary and the bank itself.
  </p>

  <h2>retention and control</h2>
  <p>
    transaction history is kept as long as the personal budget needs it.
    consent can be revoked at any time from the bank's online banking or by
    deleting the API session, which immediately stops any further access.
  </p>

  <h2>contact</h2>
  <p>
    for any question about this notice: posta@davidepucci.it.
  </p>

  <p class="caption">last updated: september 2026</p>
</main>
